RootRegistry::_isOwner
├── given the packed form ([20-byte validator][scheme sig])
│   ├── when the sig is shorter than 20 bytes
│   │   └── it should return false (no revert)
│   ├── given an active scheme is installed
│   │   ├── when the named scheme verifies the signature
│   │   │   └── it should return true
│   │   └── when the named scheme rejects the signature (wrong signer)
│   │       └── it should return false
│   └── given the named scheme is not installed
│       └── it should return false
├── given the explicit form (validator + inner sig)
│   ├── given an active scheme is installed
│   │   ├── when the signature is valid for that scheme
│   │   │   └── it should return true
│   │   └── when the signature is invalid for that scheme
│   │       └── it should return false
│   └── given the scheme is not installed
│       └── it should return false
└── given an OR-set of two active schemes
    ├── when scheme A signs and is named
    │   └── it should return true (A authorizes)
    ├── when scheme B signs and is named
    │   └── it should return true (B authorizes)
    └── when A's signer signs but B is named
        └── it should return false (the named scheme must verify)
